><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Indeed, athletes are not&#xD;a homogenous group, and individuals from different sports&#xD;(e.g. runners vs. swimmers) possess very different lowerlimb&#xD;proportions and anthropometry. Therefore, caution&#xD;should be taken when sizing and fitting athletes with compression&#xD;garments, and the only true method of ensuring&#xD;the correct fit and pressure profile would be to create customised&#xD;compression designed for the body shape and composition&#xD;of the individual.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="4" rect="609.448975,127.161041,793.448975,219.161041"
/></highlight
